A brief timeline:

Turn    Event
28,591  Picked up the Amulet of Yendor (Dlvl.48)
29,285  Arrived at the Valley of the Dead (Dlvl.27)
29,580  Picked up a cockatrice corpse (Dlvl.10)
29,668  Arrived on the Plane of Earth
29,693  Arrived on the Plane of Air
29,732  Arrived on the Plane of Fire
29,752  Arrived on the Plane of Water
29,791  Arrived on the Astral Plane
29,816  "Your wielded cockatrice corpse rots away"
29,835  Offered the Amulet at the 2nd (neutral) High Altar

1,244 turns after picking up the Amulet of Yendor, I offered it on
astral.

It took me 694 turns to climb the 21 "mysterious force" eligible
levels of gehennom.  It took another 403 turns to go from the Valley
of the Dead to Dlvl.01, 27 levels up.  The planes took a rather
pedestrian 167 turns.  I was moving so quickly a cockatrice corpse I
picked up on Dlvl.10 made it half way through astral.

How did I do it, without intrinsic teleport or the spell of teleport
away?

The high priest of moloch started the party by dropping a c!gain
level.  Then, on teleport eligible levels, I started reading scrolls
of teleportation.  Once they ran out, off went the ring of slow
digestion and on went the ring of teleportation.  I used ^T until my
power ran out in somewhere in the upper dungeon, then I let it
recharge for the planes.  I used a wish on 2 c!gain level in medusa's
lair.  I had the spell of haste self stacked for so many turns I could
forget about it.  In the elemental plains, I used jumping on fire,
earth, and astral, and levitated through air and water.

I hope you had as much fun reading/watching it as I did playing it.

